          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            In Western European jurisdictions like Germany, France, or the UK, self-employed social security, national health, and pension contributions scale proportionally or consume 20% to 45% of gross earnings. In Bulgaria, mandatory social insurance contributions are strictly capped at a monthly maximum insurable threshold of <strong>3,750 BGN (~$2,080 USD)</strong>. Any revenue or dividend distribution generated above this monthly benchmark incurs zero additional social contribution.
          </p>
